# chktex configuration for this conjecture. Run from this directory:
#
#     chktex -q statement.tex
#
# Six warnings are suppressed, checked hit by hit on 27 August 2026 rather
# than assumed, each with a 100% false-positive rate in this file:
#
#   3   "You should enclose the previous parenthesis with `{}'." Fires on literal
#       set, tuple and sign notation carrying a sub- or superscript ---
#       $\{0,1\}^{\ell}$, $(-1)^{\langle\cdot,\cdot\rangle}$,
#       $(1-2p)^{r}$, $(\pi \circ H + H)_{\pi}$ --- where the script attaches
#       to the closing delimiter exactly as intended.  (6 hits)
#   8   "Wrong length of dash may have been used." Every hit is an en-dash
#       joining two surnames (Reed--Solomon, Guruswami--Sudan,
#       DEEP-FRI's own hyphenation aside), which is this repository's
#       standing convention; chktex cannot tell a name-joining en-dash
#       from a mis-set hyphen.  (10 hits)
#   9   "`)' expected, found `]'." Fires on the half-open interval
#       $(0, (1-\rho)/2]$ the source's own theorem quantifies over.  (1 hit)
#   13  "Intersentence spacing (`\@') should perhaps be used." Every remaining
#       hit is a `:' after an uppercase letter, inside a cited title, where
#       `\@' has no effect --- TeX's spacefactor logic applies only to `.',
#       `?' and `!'. The sentence-final `.' hits were fixed with `\@'
#       rather than suppressed, and lacheck is silent.  (1 hit)
#   17  "Number of `(' doesn't match the number of `)'." Counted across the whole
#       file, so reported once at the end. Follows from 9 and is the same
#       false positive.  (2 hits)
#   24  "Delete this space to maintain correct pagereferences." Fires on
#       \label{...} sitting on its own line after \begin{definition}[...],
#       which is this repository's convention.  (2 hits)
#
# Everything else stays on. As of 27 August 2026 the file is clean under this
# config and `lacheck statement.tex` is silent.

CmdLine
{
    -n3
    -n8
    -n9
    -n13
    -n17
    -n24
}
